(  Is the supply fixed?) Tj T*
(    No. The supply can be minted, so what you hold is a share of something that can grow. Minting is not) Tj T*
(    inherently bad; unminted-and-unbounded is what dilutes you.) Tj T*
(    seen: 0xdcdc7dd0 mint\(address,uint256,bytes,bytes\), 0xaa271e1a isMinter\(address\), 0x983b2d56) Tj T*
(    addMinter\(address\)) Tj T*
(    not answered here: Whether there is a cap, and who holds the mint key.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  Who is in charge?) Tj T*
(    A single address holds admin rights, and the handover takes two steps, which is the safer version,) Tj T*
(    and that address is not visible from bytecode at all.) Tj T*
(    seen: 0x8da5cb5b owner\(\), 0xf2fde38b transferOwnership\(address\), 0x8f32d59b isOwner\(\)) Tj T*
(    not answered here: Whether that address is an EOA, a multisig or a timelock. Check it before) Tj T*
(    trusting the admin.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  Can whoever runs it take the money?) Tj T*
(    Partly, and on purpose: there are admin paths to move value out \(a sweep, a rescue, or a revenue) Tj T*
(    redirect\). They usually cannot touch your balance directly, but they can change where the money) Tj T*
(    goes.) Tj T*
(    seen: 0x2d07953a distributeRevenue\(\), 0x45338d63 setRevenueAddress\(address\)) Tj T*
