() Tj T*
(  Can anyone else move my balance?) Tj T*
(    Only with your approval: this is an allowance-based token, so the standing risk is what you have) Tj T*
(    approved, not what the contract can do on its own.) Tj T*
(    seen: 0x095ea7b3 approve\(address,uint256\), 0x23b872dd transferFrom\(address,address,uint256\),) Tj T*
(    0xdd62ed3e allowance\(address,address\)) Tj T*
(    not answered here: What you have approved right now - that is state, not bytecode.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  What happens when a transfer lands?) Tj T*
(    The recipient is called back mid-transfer, before the transfer returns. That is what makes a) Tj T*
(    counterparty that credits first and settles after paying re-enterable - the shape of the Lendf.Me) Tj T*
(    drain.) Tj T*
(    seen: 0x556f0dc7 granularity\(\), 0x06e48538 defaultOperators\(\), 0x9bd9bbc6) Tj T*
(    send\(address,uint256,bytes\)) Tj T*
(    not answered here: Whether any particular pool or vault you use is written safely. That is its own) Tj T*
(    scan.) Tj T*
(    related hazard: HZ-016) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  BOTTOM LINE) Tj T*
(1 of 16 registered hazards are present \(HZ-016\). That is the fingerprint, not a verdict: somebody) Tj T*
(still has to read the code, and the sharpest one has already been reproduced against this very) Tj T*
(contract, which raises it from a shape to a demonstrated behaviour.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  BEFORE YOU TRUST IT, CHECK) Tj T*
(    - Not a token bug: any contract that accepts this token must clear its credit before paying out, or) Tj T*
(    - re-enter-proof its payout path. Where the counterparty cannot be changed, deposit through a) Tj T*
(    - wrapper that uses transfer\(\) and keeps the callback off the hot path.) Tj T*
(    - Find out what the owner address actually is: an EOA, a multisig or a timelock.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(HAZARDS FOUND) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(HZ-016 A token that calls the recipient back mid-transfer drains a counterparty that settles after) Tj T*
(paying) Tj T*
(  class 6 asset-handling   CONFIRMED ON THIS TARGET) Tj T*
(  This token is an ERC777: transferring to a contract calls that contract back before the transfer) Tj T*
(  returns, resolved through the ERC1820 registry, and the ERC777 send\(\) additionally requires a contract) Tj T*
(  recipient to have registered an implementer. A counterparty that credits on deposit and only clears) Tj T*
(  the credit after paying out can therefore be re-entered by the recipient, paid twice out of one) Tj T*
(  balance, and left unable to pay the next honest depositor. The token is not at fault and is behaving) Tj T*
(  to spec. imBTC was the token in the Lendf.Me drain of 2020-04-19, roughly 25 million dollars in one) Tj T*
